[2026-03-14T19:03:40.637Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GiDw5U8dKzM5MYiMte75RA","type":"tool_result","content":"   200→- **Action**: User clicks \"All Teams\" in the workspace section\n   201→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/teams`.\n   202→\n   203→#### Test: Sidebar Members link navigates correctly\n   204→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   205→- **Action**: User clicks \"Members\" in the workspace section\n   206→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/members`.\n   207→\n   208→#### Test: Sidebar Labels link navigates correctly\n   209→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   210→- **Action**: User clicks \"Labels\" in the workspace section\n   211→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/labels`.\n   212→\n   213→#### Test: Sidebar Settings link navigates correctly\n   214→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   215→- **Action**: User clicks \"Settings\" in the workspace section\n   216→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings`.\n   217→\n   218→#### Test: Sidebar highlights current page link\n   219→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   220→- **Expected**: The \"My Issues\" link in the sidebar has an active/selected visual style (e.g., highlighted background, different text color). Other links do not have the active style.\n   221→\n   222→#### Test: Sidebar active highlight updates on navigation\n   223→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`, \"My Issues\" is highlighted\n   224→- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n   225→- **Expected**: \"Inbox\" becomes highlighted and \"My Issues\" loses its highlight.\n   226→\n   227→#### Test: Sidebar is present on all authenticated pages\n   228→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n   229→- **Action**: User navigates to `/my-issues`, then `/inbox`, then `/settings`\n   230→- **Expected**: The sidebar is visible and functional on all three pages with consistent layout and content.\n   231→\n   232→#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on login page\n   233→- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n   234→- **Action**: User navigates to `/login`\n   235→- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the login form is shown.\n   236→\n   237→#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on signup page\n   238→- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n   239→- **Action**: User navigates to `/signup`\n   240→- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the signup form is shown.\n   241→\n   242→### SidebarCollapse\n   243→\n   244→#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle button is visible\n   245→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n   246→- **Expected**: A toggle button is visible on the sidebar (e.g., a chevron-left icon or hamburger icon) that can collapse the sidebar.\n   247→\n   248→#### Test: Sidebar collapses to icon-only mode\n   249→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is fully expanded showing labels and icons\n   250→- **Action**: User clicks the sidebar collapse toggle button\n   251→- **Expected**: The sidebar collapses to icon-only mode. Navigation items show only their icons without text labels. The sidebar width is significantly reduced. The main content area expands to fill the freed space.\n   252→\n   253→#### Test: Sidebar expands from icon-only mode\n   254→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only (collapsed) mode\n   255→- **Action**: User clicks the sidebar expand toggle button\n   256→- **Expected**: The sidebar expands back to full width showing both icons and text labels. The main content area shrinks accordingly.\n   257→\n   258→#### Test: Sidebar collapse state persists across navigation\n   259→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is collapsed to icon-only mode\n   260→- **Action**: User clicks the \"My Issues\" icon in the collapsed sidebar, then clicks the \"Inbox\" icon\n   261→- **Expected**: The sidebar remains in collapsed icon-only mode through both navigations. It does not re-expand on page change.\n   262→\n   263→#### Test: Sidebar icons are still clickable in collapsed mode\n   264→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode, user is on `/my-issues`\n   265→- **Action**: User clicks the Inbox icon in the collapsed sidebar\n   266→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The navigation works identically to the expanded sidebar.\n   267→\n   268→#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle works multiple times in sequence\n   269→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n   270→- **Action**: User clicks the collapse toggle, then clicks it again, then clicks it once more\n   271→- **Expected**: Sidebar collapses, then expands, then collapses again. Each transition is smooth (animated, ~150ms). The toggle works reliably on repeated use.\n   272→\n   273→#### Test: Sidebar team sections visible in collapsed mode\n   274→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode, workspace has team \"Engineering\"\n   275→- **Expected**: Team navigation items are still accessible in icon-only mode (icons for Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, Views are visible and clickable).\n   276→\n   277→#### Test: Sidebar workspace section visible in collapsed mode\n   278→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode\n   279→- **Expected**: Workspace section items (All Projects, All Teams, Members, Labels, Settings) are visible as icons and remain clickable.\n   280→\n   281→### KeyboardShortcuts\n   282→\n   283→#### Test: Pressing C opens create issue modal\n   284→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, no modal is open, focus is not in a text input\n   285→- **Action**: User presses the \"C\" key\n   286→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens with the title field focused.\n   287→\n   288→#### Test: Pressing C does not open modal when typing in input\n   289→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, focus is in a text input field (e.g., a search field or comment box)\n   290→- **Action**: User presses the \"C\" key\n   291→- **Expected**: The character \"c\" is typed into the input field. The create issue modal does NOT open.\n   292→\n   293→#### Test: G then I navigates to My Issues\n   294→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`, focus is not in a text input\n   295→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"I\" key\n   296→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`.\n   297→\n   298→#### Test: G then N navigates to Inbox\n   299→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n   300→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"N\" key\n   301→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`.\n   302→\n   303→#### Test: G then I does not navigate when typing in input\n   304→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, focus is in a text input field\n   305→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then \"I\" key\n   306→- **Expected**: The characters \"gi\" are typed into the input. No navigation occurs.\n   307→\n   308→#### Test: G chord times out if second key is delayed\n   309→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n   310→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, waits 2 seconds, then presses \"I\" key\n   311→- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The chord is cancelled after a short timeout (~1 second).\n   312→\n   313→#### Test: G followed by unrecognized key does nothing\n   314→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n   315→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"X\" key\n   316→- **Expected**: Nothing happens. No navigation or modal opens. The app does not error.\n   317→\n   318→#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts work from different pages\n   319→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/settings`\n   320→- **Action**: User presses \"C\" key\n   321→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens, same as from any other page.\n   322→\n   323→#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts do not fire when modal is open\n   324→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create issue modal is open\n   325→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" then \"I\"\n   326→- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The modal remains open. The keystrokes do not trigger navigation shortcuts.\n   327→\n   328→## My Issues Page (`/my-issues`)\n   329→\n   330→**Components**: MyIssuesList, IssueRow, FiltersToolbar\n   331→\n   332→### MyIssuesList\n   333→\n   334→#### Test: My Issues page renders with issues grouped by status\n   335→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues assigned in statuses: Backlog (2 issues), In Progress (1 issue), Done (1 issue)\n   336→- **Expected**: The page displays issues grouped under status headers. Each group header shows the status icon, status name, and issue count in parentheses. Groups appear in status order: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled. Empty status groups are not displayed.\n   337→\n   338→#### Test: My Issues page shows empty state when no issues assigned\n   339→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no issues assigned to them\n   340→- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No issues assigned to you yet\") instead of an empty list.\n   341→\n   342→#### Test: Status group is collapsible\n   343→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in \"In Progress\" status, the group is expanded\n   344→- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n   345→- **Expected**: The group collapses, hiding all issues within it. The group header remains visible with a collapse indicator (e.g., chevron rotates). Clicking again expands the group back.\n   346→\n   347→#### Test: Status group collapse toggles multiple times\n   348→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group is expanded with 2 issues\n   349→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Backlog\" header to collapse, clicks it again to expand, then collapses once more"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98c1c7d5-b050-4ead-9052-211bb086d5d8","uuid":"7613b290-b160-4c6c-a181-88f487726a6a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md","content":"- **Action**: User clicks \"All Teams\" in the workspace section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/teams`.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar Members link navigates correctly\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Members\" in the workspace section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/members`.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar Labels link navigates correctly\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Labels\" in the workspace section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/labels`.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar Settings link navigates correctly\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Settings\" in the workspace section\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings`.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar highlights current page link\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n- **Expected**: The \"My Issues\" link in the sidebar has an active/selected visual style (e.g., highlighted background, different text color). Other links do not have the active style.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar active highlight updates on navigation\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`, \"My Issues\" is highlighted\n- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n- **Expected**: \"Inbox\" becomes highlighted and \"My Issues\" loses its highlight.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar is present on all authenticated pages\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n- **Action**: User navigates to `/my-issues`, then `/inbox`, then `/settings`\n- **Expected**: The sidebar is visible and functional on all three pages with consistent layout and content.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on login page\n- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n- **Action**: User navigates to `/login`\n- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the login form is shown.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on signup page\n- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n- **Action**: User navigates to `/signup`\n- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the signup form is shown.\n\n### SidebarCollapse\n\n#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle button is visible\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n- **Expected**: A toggle button is visible on the sidebar (e.g., a chevron-left icon or hamburger icon) that can collapse the sidebar.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar collapses to icon-only mode\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is fully expanded showing labels and icons\n- **Action**: User clicks the sidebar collapse toggle button\n- **Expected**: The sidebar collapses to icon-only mode. Navigation items show only their icons without text labels. The sidebar width is significantly reduced. The main content area expands to fill the freed space.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar expands from icon-only mode\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only (collapsed) mode\n- **Action**: User clicks the sidebar expand toggle button\n- **Expected**: The sidebar expands back to full width showing both icons and text labels. The main content area shrinks accordingly.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar collapse state persists across navigation\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is collapsed to icon-only mode\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"My Issues\" icon in the collapsed sidebar, then clicks the \"Inbox\" icon\n- **Expected**: The sidebar remains in collapsed icon-only mode through both navigations. It does not re-expand on page change.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar icons are still clickable in collapsed mode\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode, user is on `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks the Inbox icon in the collapsed sidebar\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The navigation works identically to the expanded sidebar.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle works multiple times in sequence\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n- **Action**: User clicks the collapse toggle, then clicks it again, then clicks it once more\n- **Expected**: Sidebar collapses, then expands, then collapses again. Each transition is smooth (animated, ~150ms). The toggle works reliably on repeated use.\n\n#### Test: Sidebar team sections visible in collapsed mode\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode, workspace has team \"Engineering\"\n- **Expected**: Team navigation items are still accessible in icon-only mode (icons for Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, Views are visible and clickable).\n\n#### Test: Sidebar workspace section visible in collapsed mode\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode\n- **Expected**: Workspace section items (All Projects, All Teams, Members, Labels, Settings) are visible as icons and remain clickable.\n\n### KeyboardShortcuts\n\n#### Test: Pressing C opens create issue modal\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, no modal is open, focus is not in a text input\n- **Action**: User presses the \"C\" key\n- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens with the title field focused.\n\n#### Test: Pressing C does not open modal when typing in input\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, focus is in a text input field (e.g., a search field or comment box)\n- **Action**: User presses the \"C\" key\n- **Expected**: The character \"c\" is typed into the input field. The create issue modal does NOT open.\n\n#### Test: G then I navigates to My Issues\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`, focus is not in a text input\n- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"I\" key\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`.\n\n#### Test: G then N navigates to Inbox\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"N\" key\n- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`.\n\n#### Test: G then I does not navigate when typing in input\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, focus is in a text input field\n- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then \"I\" key\n- **Expected**: The characters \"gi\" are typed into the input. No navigation occurs.\n\n#### Test: G chord times out if second key is delayed\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, waits 2 seconds, then presses \"I\" key\n- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The chord is cancelled after a short timeout (~1 second).\n\n#### Test: G followed by unrecognized key does nothing\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"X\" key\n- **Expected**: Nothing happens. No navigation or modal opens. The app does not error.\n\n#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts work from different pages\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/settings`\n- **Action**: User presses \"C\" key\n- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens, same as from any other page.\n\n#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts do not fire when modal is open\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create issue modal is open\n- **Action**: User presses \"G\" then \"I\"\n- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The modal remains open. The keystrokes do not trigger navigation shortcuts.\n\n## My Issues Page (`/my-issues`)\n\n**Components**: MyIssuesList, IssueRow, FiltersToolbar\n\n### MyIssuesList\n\n#### Test: My Issues page renders with issues grouped by status\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues assigned in statuses: Backlog (2 issues), In Progress (1 issue), Done (1 issue)\n- **Expected**: The page displays issues grouped under status headers. Each group header shows the status icon, status name, and issue count in parentheses. Groups appear in status order: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled. Empty status groups are not displayed.\n\n#### Test: My Issues page shows empty state when no issues assigned\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no issues assigned to them\n- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No issues assigned to you yet\") instead of an empty list.\n\n#### Test: Status group is collapsible\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in \"In Progress\" status, the group is expanded\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n- **Expected**: The group collapses, hiding all issues within it. The group header remains visible with a collapse indicator (e.g., chevron rotates). Clicking again expands the group back.\n\n#### Test: Status group collapse toggles multiple times\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group is expanded with 2 issues\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Backlog\" header to collapse, clicks it again to expand, then collapses once more","numLines":150,"startLine":200,"totalLines":2686}}}
