tions with authentication, and then build out the sidebar components that depend on them. Now I'm clarifying what the sidebar actually needs - workspace data, teams list, notification count, and route-based active highlighting. I'll set up Redux slices for UI state, teams, workspace info, and notifications, then create the corresponding Netlify functions to fetch this data.\n\nI need to make sure the RootState type includes all these slices alongside the existing auth slice, so the components can properly access everything from the store.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the implementation approach - I should follow the existing pattern from LoginForm with plain CSS and CSS variables rather than shadcn, and I'll use lucide-react for the icons since that's a common choice for this style of app.\n\nLet me start writing out all the necessary files systematically, beginning with the Redux slices and then moving into the components.\n\nFor the Sidebar structure, I'm mapping out a collapsible navigation with sections for personal items like \"My Issues\" and \"Inbox\", then team sections below that...\n\nBuilding the sidebar navigation... Writing keyboard shortcut handler... Writing the Redux slices and API functions...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":43055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":623,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98c1c7d5-b050-4ead-9052-211bb086d5d8","uuid":"45ecc0bc-c2e1-4e46-aa08-fbcf91bb5cd6"}
